# CourseVault API — every endpoint. VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ format.
# Fill in @userId / @instructorId / @courseId from the Location headers.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@instructorId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@courseId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Health — liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Ready — runs SELECT 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/ready

### OpenAPI document
GET http://localhost:4000/openapi.json

### Scalar reference (open in a browser)
# GET http://localhost:4000/reference

### ---- Users ----

### List users (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=5

### List users with filters + SQL inspector
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=instructor&q=ada&page=1&limit=10&inspect=1

### Create a user -> 201 + Location
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara Ahmed",
  "email": "sara@example.com",
  "role": "instructor"
}

### Get a user with profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}

### Replace a user (PUT = full UPDATE)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara Khan",
  "email": "sara.khan@example.com",
  "role": "instructor"
}

### Patch a user (PATCH = partial UPDATE)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara Qureshi"
}

### Delete a user -> 204 (409 if instructor still has courses)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}

### ---- Profiles (1:1) ----

### Get a profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile

### Upsert a profile (PUT = INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "PostgreSQL enthusiast.",
  "country": "Pakistan",
  "age": 24
}

### Upsert with an invalid age -> 422 from the DB CHECK (final source of truth)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "age": 200
}

### ---- Courses ----

### List courses
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?page=1&limit=5

### List courses with filters + SQL inspector
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?level=beginner&q=sql&inspect=1

### Create a course -> 201 + Location
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "instructorId": "{{instructorId}}",
  "title": "PostgreSQL Fundamentals",
  "description": "Tables, keys, constraints and JOINs.",
  "level": "beginner",
  "seats": 40,
  "startDate": "2026-11-10"
}

### Get a course with instructor + enrolledCount
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}

### Replace a course
PUT {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "instructorId": "{{instructorId}}",
  "title": "PostgreSQL Fundamentals",
  "description": "Updated description.",
  "level": "intermediate",
  "seats": 30,
  "startDate": "2026-11-10"
}

### Patch a course
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "seats": 35
}

### Delete a course -> 204 (enrollments cascade)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}

### ---- Enrollments (M:M junction) ----

### Course roster with learner details
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}/enrollments

### Enroll a learner -> 201 + Location (409 when full or duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}"
}

### Remove an enrollment -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}/enrollments/{{userId}}

### A learner's enrollments with course details
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/enrollments

### ---- Aggregates & introspection ----

### Dashboard stats (JOIN + GROUP BY)
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats

### Schema introspection for the ER diagram
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema

### ---- Injection lab ----

### Naive (display only) vs parameterized (executed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab/injection-demo
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "' OR '1'='1"
}

### Classic bypass attempt
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab/injection-demo
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "' OR 1=1 --"
}

### Stacked-query attempt
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab/injection-demo
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "'; DROP TABLE users; --"
}

### ---- Error shapes ----

### Malformed UUID -> 400 problem+json
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/not-a-uuid

### Unknown id -> 404 problem+json
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000

### Unknown route -> 404 problem+json
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Validation failure -> 400 problem+json
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{}
